# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/engine-reuse four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of the window's combined branch and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-engine-reuse-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the combined branch (the W2 + Lever N + prefix route with engine reuse merged
# in); substitute it in every template with one command (sed -i 's/tp4-engine-reuse-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every
# template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C1 (ER1 b, e and ER2's abort rows): the same tests on the audited parked arm. READ: c2_smoke_check clean; parked_compare.py against C0 (--profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-parked-audit) exits 0: concurrent streams equal the control's
# answer for answer; every abort row's reuse completes; no unpark outside the script; every rebind digest clean. Stop rule.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-engine-reuse-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-parked-audit
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,parked_churn,parked_abort_reuse
